{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784668541,"nonce":"yckW/2CTyaaeGNDuvvn2zkO8sUA=","title":"b4 config: trusts working-tree .b4-config from an applied series","message":"## Problem\n\nb4 loads the project-level `.b4-config` from the working tree in\n`_setup_main_config()` (`src/b4/__init__.py`), reading it from\n`git_get_toplevel()` at CLI startup. A curated allowlist (`wtglobs`) limits\nwhich keys a repo-shipped `.b4-config` may set, precisely because the file\ntravels with the repository and may come from an untrusted source.\n\nThe gap: `b4 review` (and `b4 am`/`b4 shazam`) *apply the series under review\ninto the working tree*. `b4 review` builds an am-ready mbox and git-am's it\nonto a `b4/review/\u003cchange_id\u003e` branch. A malicious series can include a hunk\nthat creates or modifies `.b4-config` at the repo root. Once that branch is\nchecked out, any *subsequent* b4 process loads the attacker's `.b4-config`\nand applies the allowlist to attacker-chosen values.\n\n## Concrete vector (review checks)\n\n1. Attacker submits a series containing a `.b4-config` hunk that sets a\n   hostile check command.\n2. Maintainer reviews it (`r`) -\u003e series applied to `b4/review/\u003cchange_id\u003e`,\n   checked out in the working tree. Safe during this session: `MAIN_CONFIG`\n   was loaded once at startup from the trusted checkout, before the apply.\n3. Maintainer re-runs `b4 review` while still on the review branch -- the\n   \"already on a review branch\" fast path in `review_tui/_entry.py` -- so\n   `_setup_main_config()` now reads the poisoned `.b4-config`.\n4. Running checks (`c`) executes the attacker's command\n   (`CheckRunnerMixin` -\u003e `load_check_cmds` -\u003e `_run_external_cmd`).\n\nSame class as bugzilla 218877, which commit f00a9d1 closed for\n`am-*-check-cmd` by keeping it off the allowlist.\n\n## Narrow mitigation already landed\n\n`review-*-check-cmd` was removed from the `.b4-config` allowlist in commit\n0c4cec6 (\"config: don't accept review-*-check-cmd from .b4-config\"). That\ncloses the acute review-check vector, but does not fix the root cause: other\nallowlisted command keys (`prep-*-check-cmd`, `send-auto-to-cmd`,\n`send-auto-cc-cmd`) are still attacker-influenced once a malicious series is\nchecked out and a fresh b4 process runs in that tree.\n\n## Considered broader fix\n\nStop trusting the working-tree `.b4-config` when it can be attacker-\ncontrolled. Two shapes considered:\n\n1. Ignore the worktree `.b4-config` when HEAD is a `b4/review/*` (or\n   mid-`am`) branch. Small and surgical; mirrors how `find_base` already\n   special-cases `refs/heads/b4/review/*`. Closes the review/am re-entry\n   path directly.\n2. Source `.b4-config` from a trusted ref rather than the checked-out tip --\n   e.g. read it via `git cat-file` from the review target/base branch, never\n   from the applied series. More complete (covers any applied-series\n   scenario) but more invasive to `_setup_main_config`'s sourcing.\n\nPreference: (1) as the near-term hardening, (2) as the fuller follow-up.","files":null}]}